WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.002
-The president's
political position

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.904
is eroding faster
than ever before

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.940
after a shocking testimony
from a key witness

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.307
in the impeachment inquiry.

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:10.209
for more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:11.577
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.581 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.849
There's long been a belief
in the political world

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.085
that somehow Donald Trump
is untouchable,

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.787
that he never pays
a political price for anything,

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.356
and that nothing
can ever hurt him.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.558
People like to call him
"Teflon Don."

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.594
But he doesn't look like Teflon.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:30.162
It's more like someone
made a beanbag chair

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:31.564
out of old pumpkins.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:32.765
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:34.334
Of course, the reality has
always been

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:37.036
that Trump's deeply unpopular
among majority of Americans.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.370
It's just that we're clinging

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.539
to an antiquated electoral
college system

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:42.909
that lets like five states
decide the election

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.911
and often gives the presidency

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.846
to whoever gets
the second-most votes.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.082
Nothing else in the world
works like that.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.617
Just imagine how bad "Jeopardy"
would be

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:54.621
if whoever got the lowest score
was invited back the next day.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.521
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:57.857
Okay, Donald, you got -$1,000.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.191
Looks like you're
coming back tomorrow.

00:00:59.191 --> 00:01:01.761
[ As Trump ] I hope tomorrow,
you let me by a vowel.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:02.861
[ Normal voice ]
That's a different show.

00:01:02.861 --> 00:01:04.831
[ As Trump ] Whatever.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.733
I want that vowel.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.770
J.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.739
[ Normal voice ] But still
it really feels like

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:15.508
we're seeing a potentially major
political shift

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.943
happen right now
with impeachment.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.779
A new CNN poll yesterday found
that the highest number yet,

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:23.516
a full 50% of Americans want the
president not just impeached,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.518
but removed from office
altogether.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.020
-Just out this morning,
a brand-new CNN poll

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.323
finds public support
for impeaching

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:33.259
and removing President Trump
from office on the rise.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.927
-Here's that numeric high.

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:37.664
50%,
half the country in this poll,

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:40.332
"Should Trump be impeached
and removed from office?"

00:01:40.332 --> 00:01:44.370
50% say yes. 43% say no.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.105
Take a look at this over time,

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.808
and you'll see that
it's the high water mark.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.242
-Hey, you've got to give it
to Trump.

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:52.545
This is definitely the first
time in his life

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:55.214
he's ever hit a high water mark.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:57.783
Trump spent most of his life
at the low water mark,

00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:00.420
which makes sense because
he does kind of look like

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.887
something you would find
on the beach

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:03.389
after the tide goes out.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.523
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:06.125
[ As Trump ]
Please push me in the water

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:08.294
so I can rejoin my pod.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.595
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.764
[ Normal voice ] And you know
Trump saw that CNN poll,

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.666
because he watches cable news
all the time.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.302
His staff probably had to edit
the clip on his DVR

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.470
and hope he didn't notice.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.240
-A brand-new CNN poll
finds public support

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.208
for President Trump on the rise.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.076
-Take a look at this.
It's the high water mark.

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:25.711
50%...
-Support...

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:26.946
-...Trump.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.482
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.650
-[ As Trump ]
I don't know why everyone

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.418
is jumping at this poll.
It's great!

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.054
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.656
[ Normal voice ]
So Trump's political position

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.924
is eroding quickly
and we're even starting to see

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:41.294
some small cracks in his support
among Republicans.

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:44.163
Retiring Florida Congressman
Francis Rooney said

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:45.798
he wouldn't rule out
voting for impeachment,

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.134
and Utah Senator Mitt Romney
said this

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.937
about Trump's quid pro quo
with Ukraine on Sunday.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.471
-We certainly
can't have presidents

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:55.441
asking foreign countries
to provide something

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.742
of political value.

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:58.544
That is, after all,
against the law.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.179
-Yeah, it is,
and I can't believe

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:01.647
that even has to be said.

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:03.449
It's like if you were doing
120 on the highway

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.150
while snorting cocaine,
drinking tequila,

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.886
and mooning other drivers, and
a cap pulled you over and said,

00:03:07.886 --> 00:03:10.323
"Public nudity, after all,
is against the law."

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.824
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.959
Of course, after Romney
made those comments,

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:16.195
Trump, who demands absolute
loyalty from everyone,

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:19.264
lashed out at him on Monday
suggesting that Democrats

00:03:19.264 --> 00:03:20.833
were better at sticking
together.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.668
-I think the Democrats
fight dirty,

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.905
but two things they have --
they're vicious,

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.940
and they stick together.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.376
They don't have Mitt Romney
in their midst.

00:03:31.376 --> 00:03:32.945
They don't have
people like that.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:34.647
-All right, first of all,
the idea that Democrats

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.316
don't disagree with each other
is insane.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:37.516
[ Laughter ]
I mean,

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:39.018
the difference is that
when Democrats argue,

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.887
they have productive
disagreements over things

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.555
like how to provide healthcare
to everyone

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.290
or how to address
institutional racism.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.624
When Republicans argue,
it's like the end

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:46.993
of a botched bank robbery

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.828
where everyone is pointing guns
at each other, screaming,

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.262
"Who's the ride?
Are you the ride?

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:53.132
I'm not the ri--
Oh, we're so [bleep]"

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:55.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:58.771
That's why Trump is lashing out
in increasingly deranged ways

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.373
because he doesn't have
an actual defense.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.874
He and his aides have already
confessed

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.408
to the crimes in question.

00:04:03.408 --> 00:04:06.078
The facts have been so brutal
for Trump and his team

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:08.080
that in less than a month,
they went from this...

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.684
-There was no quid pro quo.
-To this...

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.453
-What exactly did you hope
Zelensky would do

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:16.855
about the Bidens
after your phone call?

00:04:16.855 --> 00:04:20.659
-Well, I would think that
if they were honest about it,

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:23.862
they'd start a major
investigation into the Bidens.

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:26.098
-To this...
-So the demand for

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:27.967
an investigation
into the Democrats

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.635
was part of the reason that he

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:32.204
ordered to withhold funding
to Ukraine?

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:35.775
-The look back to what happened
in 2016

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:38.210
certainly was part of the thing
that he was worried about

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.478
in corruption with that nation,

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:40.613
and that is absolutely
appropriate.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.248
-Withholding the funding?
-Yeah.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.851
-But to be clear, what you just
described is a quid pro quo.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:48.220
It is, funding will not flow
unless the investigation

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:52.959
into the Democratic server
happened, as well.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.461
-We do --
We do that all the time.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.129
-All right, first of all --
[ Audience groans ]

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:59.332
First of all, I love Mulvaney's
face right there

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:00.466
when the reporter says,

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.635
"What you just described
is a quid pro quo."

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.570
He reacts like a guy
who just realized

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.672
he said the wrong name
during sex.

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:07.406
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:08.574
Ohh, Janet!

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.343
[ High-pitched ]
My name is Lisa.

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:13.779
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:16.215
[ Normal voice ]
You don't look like a Lisa.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.150
Second, not only did he
just admit it,

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.453
he said they do it
all the time.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:23.089
These idiots are the only
criminals in the world

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.158
who would defend themselves
from one crime

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.426
by confessing to more crimes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.729
It's like if the cops called you
in about a murder and said,

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.564
"Did you dump the body
in Central Park?"

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.032
And you went,
"Of course, I did.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.500
That's where I dump
all my bodies."

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.236
[ Laughter ]
"I assume I'm free to go?"

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.104
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:41.340
So, the Trump team --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:44.076
The Trump team's position
on Ukraine has, let's say,

00:05:44.076 --> 00:05:46.579
evolved, which makes sense,
since Trump himself

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:48.514
looks like he should be
third from the right

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.082
on one of those
human evolution charts.

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:52.851
I mean, that's why he is so much
more comfortable

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:55.354
crawling like a sea turtle
who just buried his golf balls

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:56.923
in the stand.

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:58.157
Whenever he stands upright,

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:00.293
his center gravity
shifts forward

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:04.163
like a baby standing up
in his crib.

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.698
And he even holds --

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:08.334
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:11.070
He even holds his hands out
like he's waiting for an adult

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.638
to steer him while he walks.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:15.408
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:17.343
in fact, Republicans
are flailing so badly

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.044
in their attempts to actually
defended what Trump did

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:22.181
with Ukraine, that rather
than mount an actual defense,

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:25.451
they've decided instead
to resort to dumb stunts

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:26.719
to shut down the inquiry
altogether.

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.120
Like today when a group
of Republicans

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.455
barged into a House deposition
in the secure room

00:06:30.455 --> 00:06:31.690
and refused to leave.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.160
-We start with a bizarre turn
on Capitol Hill

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.795
when as many as two dozen
House Republicans

00:06:36.795 --> 00:06:39.064
upset over
the impeachment inquiry

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:41.433
stormed a secure hearing room.

00:06:41.433 --> 00:06:44.870
Republicans physically
got in the faces of Democrats

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:46.538
to protest these proceedings.

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:47.973
-A wild scene
in Washington today

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:49.809
when two dozen
House conservative

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:52.444
stormed the impeachment
hearing room in protest

00:06:52.444 --> 00:06:53.946
and refused to leave.

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:55.548
-These guys are truly so dumb.

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:57.716
I mean, look at this group
of angry weirdos

00:06:57.716 --> 00:06:59.085
at their press conference
this morning

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:01.153
announcing they were going to
storm the hearing room.

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:03.255
I haven't seen a group
of white guys that angry

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:05.123
since they found out
their Don Henley tickets

00:07:05.123 --> 00:07:06.359
were obstructed view.

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:10.896
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:12.898
Looks like a protest
outside a pharmacy

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:14.367
that ran out of Viagra.

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:15.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.102
[ Applause ]

00:07:17.102 --> 00:07:19.438
And they shouldn't be
at the Capitol.

00:07:19.438 --> 00:07:21.840
They should be standing
at the counter at a McDonald's

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:23.442
demanding to see the manager.

00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:25.678
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:27.879
And even while Trump
and his team

00:07:27.879 --> 00:07:29.181
are confessing on TV,

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:31.283
Democrats in the House
are still gathering evidence

00:07:31.283 --> 00:07:32.584
as part of the impeachment
inquiry.

00:07:32.584 --> 00:07:35.554
Yesterday, the top US diplomat
in Ukraine, Bill Taylor,

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:38.691
testified that there was in fact
an explicit quid pro quo

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:41.093
in which Trump held up hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:43.996
in military aid to Ukraine
in exchange for a pledge

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:45.564
to investigate
his political rivals.

00:07:45.564 --> 00:07:47.699
According to reports,
Taylor's opening statement

00:07:47.699 --> 00:07:50.770
was 15 pages long and prompted
a lot of sighs and gasps.

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:53.572
And unless you're reading aloud
from your book of erotica,

00:07:53.572 --> 00:07:55.407
that is not good.

00:07:55.407 --> 00:07:58.110
As a general rule,
it is never good

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.812
to hear sighs or gasps.

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.514
It never means you are innocent.

00:08:02.514 --> 00:08:05.217
And there are only two reasons
why a roomful of people gasp --

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:07.252
when someone makes
a shocking accusation in court,

00:08:07.252 --> 00:08:08.621
or when you and your buddies
are watching

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:11.190
a super cut
of skateboard fails.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.292
Oh, damn.
Rudy tried to do an ollie

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.428
and got the skateboard
wedged up his ass.

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:17.896
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.896 --> 00:08:20.332
People in the room called
Taylor's testimony disturbing

00:08:20.332 --> 00:08:22.501
and said he drew a direct line
between President Trump's

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:25.404
withholding of aid for Ukraine
and his demand for investigation

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:26.772
into Joe Biden
and the Democrats.

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:29.775
And Taylor reportedly backed up
all of his assertions

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.444
with detailed notes
and evidence.

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:34.714
-He is backing up himself
in this case, Taylor is,

00:08:34.714 --> 00:08:36.449
with an opening statement
that I'm told

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:38.517
relies on meticulous notes.

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:40.953
This is apparently
a life long habit of his

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:43.956
to take meticulous notes
about meetings and phone calls

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:45.190
in which he was a participant.

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.759
So Taylor, perhaps more than
any other witness,

00:08:47.759 --> 00:08:50.496
has come with his own
paper trail in place --

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:52.431
a 15-page opening statement.

00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:55.067
-15 pages.
The only good news for Trump

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:58.437
is there is no way he's capable
of reading a 15-page document.

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:01.540
I doubt Trump ever made it all
the way through a Snapple cap.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.575
[ As Trump ] A duck's quack
does not --

00:09:03.575 --> 00:09:05.411
Somebody else read the rest
of this for me.

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:06.711
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.711 --> 00:09:09.849
Then summarize it for me
in a memo.

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:12.351
[ Normal voice ] Also, no phrase
has ever been more terrifying

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:14.453
for a guy like Trump
than the words "paper trail."

00:09:14.453 --> 00:09:16.222
He's a New York City
real-estate developer

00:09:16.222 --> 00:09:18.090
and casino owner
who cheats on his taxes.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.026
The only paper trail he's ever
kept is the toilet paper

00:09:21.026 --> 00:09:23.195
on the bottom of his shoe.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:25.864
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:25.864 --> 00:09:28.366
Trump has always thought
of himself as untouchable,

00:09:28.366 --> 00:09:30.569
but now he is finally facing
real consequences.

00:09:30.569 --> 00:09:32.505
Support for impeachment
is rising in the polls.

00:09:32.505 --> 00:09:34.340
More and more people
are coming to the conclusion

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.374
that you can't just subvert

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:37.209
the entirety of American
foreign policy

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:38.878
to your personal political will

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:40.980
and dangle hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.682
as part of a corrupt
quid pro quo

00:09:42.682 --> 00:09:44.283
to investigate
your political rivals.

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:45.684
Because, to put it mildly...

00:09:45.684 --> 00:09:47.686
-That is, after all,
against the law.

00:09:47.686 --> 00:09:48.921
